      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Labor market dynamics vary significantly across these regions. Generally, Southeast Asia often offers mature manufacturing bases with established supply chain practices, while Eastern Europe blends European standards with lower costs. Sub-Saharan Africa presents the highest variability, with skilled labor shortages but rapidly improving availability in certain tech hubs. Expect lower initial hands-on management requirements in established SEA hubs, but potentially higher oversight needs in emerging markets like parts of SSA.",
