      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Culturally, Eastern European workforces often exhibit a strong inclination toward direct adherence to established processes, fitting a more directive management style well. In contrast, some Southeast Asian cultures value consensus and group dynamics, which can require more coaching before trainees master complex independent tasks. Sub-Saharan African workforces show the broadest spectrum; success often depends heavily on the specific local infrastructure and management approach implemented.",
